body:
I think that the PR that causes this issue is probably #9735.

After executing _injectScope, the "include" attribute of "options" variable of  are different between v5.0.0-beta13 and v5.0.0-beta14. 
https://github.com/sequelize/sequelize/blob/11f56fcd7050712c33c867589d4e5086a86b4a1c/lib/model.js#L1704

However, I can't judge whether it is a regression.
@frlinw @sushantdhiman What do you think?

BTW when using "model" param instead of "association", the code seems to work fine in v5.0.0-beta14.
```
    include: [
      {
        model: Mission,
        attributes: ['id'],
        where: {
          startDate: {
            [Sequelize.Op.gte]: new Date(),
            [Sequelize.Op.lte]: new Date()
          }
        }
      },
      {
        model: Building,
        attributes: ['id']
      }
    ]
```

Thanks @tsasaki609 ! 
@u9r52sld can you confirm [your rework](https://github.com/sequelize/sequelize/pull/9735/files#diff-a140b60b6a99a8c69f4b5d0d1f1f2bfaR3081) just removed the particular treatment of `association` ?
Maybe tests for the `association` property should be added
